<title>THAILAND: Thai bourse allows Sanyo trade resumption.</title>
<headline>Thai bourse allows Sanyo trade resumption.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1996-12-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Stock Exchange of Thailand said trading would resume in the shares of suspended Sanyo Universal Electric Plc in the afternoon session on Thursday.</p>
<p>It said in a statement this was because the company had reported fully on the Tuesday arson attack on its warehouse and head office in the eastern outskirts of Bangkok by a group of disgruntled workers angry over reduced year-end bonuses.  </p>
<p>Sanyo Universal had told the stock exchange that its production line was unaffected by the fire.</p>
<p>The company, which produces refrigerators as well as a range of household appliances, said the fire had affected sales only slightly because goods in stock were sufficient for delivery to most customers.</p>
<p>Sanyo Universal shares closed unchanged at 75.50 baht on December 17.</p>
<p>Police have arrested and charged six workers in connection with the arson on the Sanyo property.</p>
<p>-- Bangkok newsroom (662) 652-0642</p>
